#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "CAP-ENVIRONMENTS Environments by branching"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "An environment is a template plus values; development is isolated inside production by branching."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "Layer L1 · domain: movement · depends on: [CAP-OPERATIONALDB]{1}, [CAP-CATALOG]{2}."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "Isolate development and testing from production, with or without a second funded environment."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "Isolation means no development write reaches production data and no consumer reads development output; branches and ungranted schemas give that inside one environment ([P7]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "A template and one values file per environment."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "Per-change database branches and development schemas with a time to live."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "A database branch does not branch object storage. A branch that writes files would write them into production storage, so branches get their own storage and read production storage read-only."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "Contract"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "Clause"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "Level"
msgstr ""

