msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "CAP-ENVIRONMENTS.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "An environment is one template plus one values file, and every axis agrees which environment it is: catalog and schema, database branch and database, application identity and configuration, and jobs."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "Each application's health endpoint (CAP-APPS.2) matches its values file."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "CAP-ENVIRONMENTS.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "Without a funded development environment, development is isolated inside production: database branches, and development schemas in production catalogs with no consumer grants."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "Development objects exist only as branches and ungranted schemas."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "CAP-ENVIRONMENTS.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "A branch never writes to production object storage. Branches use their own storage, and may read production storage only through a read-only path.{1}*Example:* A developer's branch can read production's scanned documents to test a change, but an upload attempted from the branch is refused."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "A write to production storage from a branch's identity is refused."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "CAP-ENVIRONMENTS.4"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "Each change under review gets its own branch and development schemas with a time to live, removed when the change merges."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "After merge, the change's branch and schemas are gone."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "CAP-ENVIRONMENTS.5"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "Grants and identities are declared per environment; the same configuration never implies the same securable."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-environments.md
msgid "Each environment's grants are listed separately in its plan."
msgstr ""

